{
  "dom_id": "step-q131289",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨{y}^{2}z,{x}^{2}+z,{x}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨1,1,-1⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(x+y-z)\\cdot 0+⟨{y}^{2}z,{x}^{2}+z,{x}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =0+{y}^{2}z+{x}^{2}+z-{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}z+z \\\\  & =z({y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
